cpass2

tldr
	Minimal password manager. C99, OpenSSL.
	scrypt key derivation, AES-256-GCM encryption.
	One file per entry, random file names, real names only in encrypted MAIN.
	Master password is the only secret.

entry format
	password
	username
	website
	extra (free text, any number of lines)

commands
	cpass2 init		create store, set master password
	cpass2 add NAME		add entry (NAME may be Dir/site.com)
	cpass2 get NAME		print entry, password first
	cpass2 ls		list entries as a tree
	cpass2 edit NAME	edit entry in $EDITOR
	cpass2 rm NAME		remove entry
	cpass2 copy NAME	password to clipboard, prints [in clipboard]

compile
	cc -std=c99 -O2 -Wall -o cpass2 cpass2.c -lcrypto

	clipboard command (default xclip -selection clipboard):
	cc -std=c99 -O2 -Wall -DCPASS2_CLIP=\"xsel\ -bi\" -o cpass2 cpass2.c -lcrypto

install
	install -m 755 cpass2 /usr/local/bin/cpass2

	as a pass replacement:
	install -m 755 cpass2 /usr/local/bin/pass

environment
	CPASS2_DIR	store directory, default ~/.cpass2/
	EDITOR		used by edit, default vi

files
	salt		16 byte scrypt salt
	MAIN		encrypted index (id -> name)
	<hex id>	encrypted entry
